+# Vanta Forge patch integration report
+
+Base: `Ronin-Vanta-Android-0.18.1-RC1-source.zip`.
+Patch: `Vanta-Forge-Fix.zip`.
+
+**Edits applied to:**
+- `app/src/main/java/com/ronin/vanta/ForgeCodeDiagnostics.java`
+- `app/src/main/java/com/ronin/vanta/ForgeAuthor.java`
+- `app/src/main/java/com/ronin/vanta/AgenticRepair.java`
+- `app/src/main/java/com/ronin/vanta/AndroidProjectCheck.java`
+- `app/build.gradle` (`versionCode 182`, `versionName 0.18.1-rc2`)
+
+**Added:**
+- `app/src/main/java/com/ronin/vanta/ForgeSourceGuard.java`
+- `app/src/main/java/com/ronin/vanta/ForgeDiagnosticPatterns.java`
+- `app/src/test/java/com/ronin/vanta/ForgeSourceGuardTest.java`
+- `app/src/test/java/com/ronin/vanta/ForgeDiagnosticPatternsTest.java`
+
+Existing JUnit 4 Gradle test dependency was already present.
+A false-positive regression was also corrected: Java expressions like `j.json`
+are legitimate field accesses, not pasted source-file headers.
+
+## Build
+
+In Android Studio, open this directory; sync Gradle; run `testDebugUnitTest` and
+`assembleRelease` (compile SDK 36 and JDK 17 are required).
+Sign the resulting release APK with **the same original Vanta signing key**
+through Android Studio's Generate Signed App Bundle / APK workflow or an
+existing trusted signing process. Without that key, you cannot install this
+as an update over the existing app. `applicationId` is unchanged.
+
+Build completion, unit tests and app-update compatibility must be verified on a
+machine with Android SDK 36, Gradle deps and the matching signing identity.
